(SECURE C# MCP AGENT DEMO - ARCHITECTURE) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Version: 1.1) Tj
T*
(Audience: Security engineers and .NET architects) Tj
T*
(Date: May 2026) Tj
T*
(Status: Demo / educational) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Executive Summary) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This project demonstrates a secure-by-default shape for a small MCP-style release-) Tj
T*
(  assessment server and a rule-based console client. It is built with .NET 8 and focuses) Tj
T*
(  on auth boundaries, scope checks, consistent tool discovery, auditable tool calls, and) Tj
T*
(  negative-path tests.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The system is not production-ready identity infrastructure. The token issuer and secrets) Tj
T*
(  are intentionally local demo mechanisms.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Components) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(| Component | Responsibility | Security control |) Tj
T*
(| --- | --- | --- |) Tj
T*
(| `SecureMcpServer` | ASP.NET Core Minimal API host for auth, SSE, JSON-RPC messages,) Tj
T*
(  and tool discovery | JWT bearer auth and scope policies |) Tj
T*
(| `DemoTokenService` | Issues and validates demo JWTs | issuer, audience, signing key,) Tj
T*
(  lifetime validation |) Tj
T*
(| `ReleaseDataService` | Serves release status, dependencies, vulnerability data, and) Tj
T*
(  release approval | checks `mcp:tools:release` before approval |) Tj
T*
(| `SecurityAuditLogger` | Logs auth success/failure, tool calls, and tool errors |) Tj
T*
(  structured application logs |) Tj
T*
(| `SecureMcpClient` | Console client with a simple rule-based planner | obtains token) Tj
T*
(  and delegates auth decisions to the server |) Tj
T*
(| `demo-data.json` | Self-contained release data for deterministic responses | copied to) Tj
T*
(  build output |) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Endpoint Model) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(| Endpoint | Method | Purpose | Auth |) Tj
T*
(| --- | --- | --- | --- |) Tj
T*
(| `/auth/token` | POST | Demo-only JWT issuance | validates requested scopes and demo) Tj
T*
(  release secret |) Tj
T*
(| `/mcp/sse` | GET | SSE endpoint advertisement | requires `mcp:tools` |) Tj
T*
(| `/mcp/messages` | POST | JSON-RPC `tools/list` and `tools/call` | requires) Tj
T*
(  `mcp:tools`; `approve_release` also requires `mcp:tools:release` |) Tj
T*
(| `/mcp/tools` | GET | Declarative tool discovery | requires `mcp:tools` |) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The SSE endpoint advertises `/mcp/messages` without embedding the bearer token in the) Tj
T*
(  URL. Clients should continue to send the token in the `Authorization` header.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Tool Contract) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(`/mcp/tools` and `tools/list` expose the same four implemented tools:) Tj
T*
() Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
